rajesh and atul gupta fled south africa  in 2018 after being charged with fraud  corruption and money laundering  although an interpol red notice has led  to the arrest of the brothers in dubai  it may be some time before they're  extradited presumably these these  suspects will be brought before a court  and they will then  utilize their rights to  try to resist the extradition  but if  if their petition to uh stop the  extradition is not successful then we  would expect to see that uh  that request ratified uh by the relevant  authorities and then for them to be  physically put on a plane and brought  back to south africa but it could it  could take some time  the guptas immigrated from india to  south africa in the early 1990s  their relationship with former president  jacob zuma is at the center of the  scandal surrounding the family zuma was  forced to resign in 2018 following  pressure from within his party it's  alleged the guptas influenced government  policy and the appointment of cabinet  ministers and looted state funds  an estimated 32 billion dollars was  stolen during zuma's nine years in  office  the former president is facing a  separate trial on charges of fraud  linked to a multi-million dollar arms  deal other gupta family members and  associates are currently on trial for  allegedly siphoning off state funds  meant for a farming project the gupta  brothers are also implicated many south  africans have welcomed the arrest but  political commentators say allegations  of corruption at the highest levels of  government may not be limited to the  zuma administration current president  sul ramaphosa is facing his own scandal  he's accused of failing to report the  2020 theft of up to four million dollars  from his farm in the limpopo province  family al jazeera johannesburg
 

